q
1 0 0 1 42 681.3898 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 28.5 Tm 12.5 TL /F1 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (We chose the ) Tj /F2 9 Tf (Layered \(Three-Tier\) Architecture) Tj /F1 9 Tf ( for the EV Charging Station Reservation System. The system is decoupled) Tj T* (into three cohesive tiers \227 Presentation, Business Logic, and Data Persistence \227 where each tier communicates only with the) Tj T* (adjacent tier through well-defined interfaces.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 659.3898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 11 Tf 14 TL (2. Reason 1: Transactional Integrity Across Coupled Operations) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 581.3898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 66 Tm /F1 9 Tf 12.5 TL (Reserving a charger is inherently transactional: the system must verify that the charger is operational and connector-compatible,) Tj T* (confirm that the time slot is unreserved, create the reservation record, lock the interval, and queue a confirmation notification.) Tj T* -0.025201 Tw (These steps must succeed or fail together. A centralized data access layer backed by ACID-compliant relational transactions \(for) Tj T* 0 Tw (example, a uniqueness constraint or row-level lock on charger and time slot\) prevents double-booking even when two drivers) Tj T* (confirm the same slot simultaneously. A microservices design with a separate data store per service would need saga-style) Tj T* (compensating transactions to give the same guarantee, which adds complexity this application does not need.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 559.3898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 11 Tf 14 TL (3. Reason 2: Shared Domain Logic Across Two Role Portals) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 493.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 53.5 Tm /F1 9 Tf 12.5 TL (The platform serves two actor classes \227 EV Drivers and Station Operators \227 whose portals have different workflows \(search) Tj T* (and reserve versus publish slots and close sessions\). Both portals, however, operate on the same entities and rules: charger) Tj T* (status, slot availability, tariffs, cancellation cut-off, and session records. Layered architecture keeps role-specific presentation) Tj T* (concerns in the Presentation tier and consolidates these rules in a single Business Logic tier, so each rule is implemented once) Tj T* (and cannot drift between the two portals.) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 471.8898 cm
q
0 0 0 rg
BT 1 0 0 1 0 3 Tm /F2 11 Tf 14 TL (4. Security Advantage: Centralized Role-Based Access Control \(RBAC\)) Tj T* ET
Q
Q
q
1 0 0 1 42 406.3898 cm
q
BT 1 0 0 1 0 53.5 Tm 12.5 TL /F1 9 Tf 0 0 0 rg (The Business Logic tier acts as a single, authoritative security boundary. Every request from either portal passes through the) Tj T* (Authentication & User Management component before it reaches reservation or session services. This choke point centralizes) Tj T* (token validation and RBAC enforcement, so drivers can access only their own reservations and receipts, and operators can) Tj T* (manage only the chargers and bookings of their own stations \(NFR-001\). Compared with a microservices deployment, there are) Tj T* (fewer network-exposed endpoints to secure and no inter-service token propagation to design and audit.) Tj T* ET
